---
/* A few fireflies over the evening photos. Michigan yards at dusk, and the one
   playful thing on the site. Drawn on a canvas that starts after the page has
   settled, so nothing here touches the first paint. They drift, pulse, and lean
   gently toward a pointer. Paused off screen and in a hidden tab, and absent for
   visitors who ask for reduced motion or for data saving. */
---

<canvas class="ff" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>


<style>
  .ff {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 1.6s ease;
  }

  .ff.is-on {
    opacity: 1;
  }
</style>
